<h2>Your account information</h2>
<p>RepairConnect stores account details in its database. Administrators can view account details, manage account status, and review technician applications according to their permissions.</p>
<h2>Signing in</h2>
<p>Passwords are stored as hashes. Signing in creates a protected session cookie that JavaScript cannot read. If you choose to stay signed in, that cookie can remain on your device after you close the browser. Sign out on shared devices.</p>
<h2>Available services</h2>
<p>Sign-up creates a Client account. Clients can apply to become technicians using that same account and upload a supporting document. Approval adds Technician access while keeping Client access. Supporting documents can be downloaded only by their owner or an administrator. Account administration and service-category management are connected to the server. Repair requests, bookings, and the public technician directory are not available yet.</p>
<h2>Browser storage</h2>
<p>The website does not store passwords, account records, or repair requests in browser local storage. It no longer uses the earlier preview records.</p>
<h2>Before public launch</h2>
<p>The service owner must publish its contact details, retention policy, and the process for requesting access to or removal of personal information.</p>
